      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm 35 and im looking to start lifting weights for the first time. can u make me a 4 week linear progression plan? i want to focus on the main compound lifts like squat, bench and deadlift. just looking for something simple to build a base.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can provide you with a 4-week linear progression plan. For beginners, a lower volume and heavier weights are recommended. Here's a plan focusing on the main compound lifts:\n\nWeek 1:\n- Monday: Squat - 3 sets of 5 reps, 60-70% 1RM\n- Tuesday: Bench Press - 3 sets of 5 reps, 60-70% 1RM\n- Thursday: Deadlift - 3 sets of 5 reps, 60-70% 1RM\n- Saturday: (Optional) Cardio day, 20-30 minutes, e.g., jogging or cycling\n\nWeek 2: Increase rep range to 3 sets of 8 reps, add 2.5-5lbs to each lift\nWeek 3: Increase rep range to 3 sets of 10 reps, add 2.5-5lbs to each lift\nWeek 4: Increase rep range to 3 sets of 12 reps, add 2.5-5lbs to each lift\n\nRemember to adjust your weight according to your comfort level and listen to your body, taking rest days as needed.",
