    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. quick question though, regarding the progress—is it normal for my energy levels to tank halfway through the workout or for my muscles to feel really weird/unsteady toward the end of a set? just wanna make sure i'm not overdoing it or something.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's normal to feel fatigued or your muscles might feel unsteady during and after the workout, especially if you're new to weightlifting. Muscle fatigue (a temporary decrease in muscle force production) and rep fatigue (increasing fatigue rate with more reps) are normal signs.\n\nIf you're feeling extremely tired, dizziness, or experiencing pain, stop the exercise immediately. However, if you notice any of these symptoms halfway through a set:\n\n- Cramping or shivering\n- Palpitations or dizziness\n- Numbness or tingling\n- Unusual pain\n\nStop and reassess your form, weight, and overall comfort level before continuing.\n\nOn the other hand, an 'unsteady\" feeling might be due to proper or improper form. If you feel unstable during a lift, re-evaluate your technique, and if it persists, consider consulting a personal trainer or coach for guidance.",
